[
    {
        "content": "<p>Hello, I <em>think</em> I understand the following, but is it actually expected?</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Julia console\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"gp\">julia&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hasmethod</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">pairs</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Tuple</span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"kt\">UnionAll</span><span class=\"p\">})</span>\n<span class=\"go\">true</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">julia&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pairs</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"gr\">ERROR: MethodError: no method matching keys(::Type{Type})</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>IIUC <code>pairs</code> is defined for that input, but it should not actually be ran. I was relying on <code>hasmethod</code> to figure whether arbitrary input could be iterated upon using <code>pairs</code>, but maybe I should ask \"forgiveness rather than permission\"?</p>",
        "id": 639765958,
        "sender_full_name": "iago-lito",
        "timestamp": 1794492645
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'm not sure I understand the question.  <code>pairs</code> is applicable to any tuple, but your second call doesn't have a tuple argument at all.</p>",
        "id": 639773559,
        "sender_full_name": "Gunnar Farnebäck",
        "timestamp": 1794494094
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>IIUC the tuple in <a href=\"https://docs.julialang.org/en/v1/base/base/#Base.hasmethod\">hasmethod</a> is just here to list the requested argument types. Here one single argument <code>Type::UnionAll</code> thus <code>Tuple{UnionAll}</code> (edited/fixed in the above)</p>",
        "id": 639774217,
        "sender_full_name": "iago-lito",
        "timestamp": 1794494212
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'm still confused but for what it's worth:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Julia\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">julia</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pairs</span><span class=\"p\">((</span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"p\">,))</span>\n<span class=\"n\">pairs</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"o\">::</span><span class=\"kt\">Tuple</span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"kt\">UnionAll</span><span class=\"p\">})</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">with</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">entry</span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 639774720,
        "sender_full_name": "Gunnar Farnebäck",
        "timestamp": 1794494303
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>My point is that I would expect <code>pairs(Type)</code> to  succeed because <code>hasmethod(pairs, Tuple{UnionAll})</code> returns <code>true</code>. It's failing though. Not because the method is undefined, but because some internal callee <code>keys</code> seems undefined.</p>",
        "id": 639775085,
        "sender_full_name": "iago-lito",
        "timestamp": 1794494374
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(Actually I would rather expect <code>hasmethod(pairs, Tuple{UnionAll})</code> to return <code>false</code> instead because <code>pairs(Type)</code> fails.)</p>",
        "id": 639775327,
        "sender_full_name": "iago-lito",
        "timestamp": 1794494419
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>To clarify: the following is less suprising:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Julia console\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"gp\">julia&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hasmethod</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">sqrt</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Tuple</span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"kt\">Int</span><span class=\"p\">})</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c\"># One argument of type `Int`.</span>\n<span class=\"go\">true</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">julia&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sqrt</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c\"># Doesn't fail.</span>\n<span class=\"go\">2.23606797749979</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 639775589,
        "sender_full_name": "iago-lito",
        "timestamp": 1794494472
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Part of my confusion was that I didn't read (or remember) the <code>hasmethod</code> docstring well enough, sorry about that.</p>\n<p>I think the general problem is that <code>pairs</code> must work for any collection or iterable, but there's no abstract type for all of those, so <code>pairs</code> needs to dispatch on <code>Any</code>. If you call it with other input it will error and the question is mostly how gracefully it does that.</p>",
        "id": 639778517,
        "sender_full_name": "Gunnar Farnebäck",
        "timestamp": 1794494994
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I see. So there is no way I can query <code>::Any</code> for being \"iterable\"?</p>",
        "id": 639778784,
        "sender_full_name": "iago-lito",
        "timestamp": 1794495039
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'm not sure how robust it is, but trying <code>hasmethod</code> on <code>iterate</code> is probably more informative.</p>",
        "id": 639779922,
        "sender_full_name": "Gunnar Farnebäck",
        "timestamp": 1794495191
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It is, but I expect to iterate over matrices using <code>pairs</code> not <code>iterate</code> (which would traverse them linearly) :\\</p>",
        "id": 639780126,
        "sender_full_name": "iago-lito",
        "timestamp": 1794495224
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I find it difficult to write generic code then ^ ^\"</p>",
        "id": 639780299,
        "sender_full_name": "iago-lito",
        "timestamp": 1794495253
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Regarding your <code>sqrt</code> example, <code>sqrt(-5)</code> does error despite having a method defined.</p>",
        "id": 639780474,
        "sender_full_name": "Gunnar Farnebäck",
        "timestamp": 1794495282
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Indeed, this is why I sort of understand the above. I also understand how <code>hasmethod</code> is not a reliable way to \"duck-type\" input.</p>",
        "id": 639780754,
        "sender_full_name": "iago-lito",
        "timestamp": 1794495323
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Note that <code>sqrt(-5)</code> fails because of the input runtime <em>value</em>, whereas <code>pairs(Type)</code> fails because of the input static <em>type</em>.</p>",
        "id": 639780964,
        "sender_full_name": "iago-lito",
        "timestamp": 1794495359
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I wish there would be a way to request whether the call is at least <em>statically</em> correct.</p>",
        "id": 639781853,
        "sender_full_name": "iago-lito",
        "timestamp": 1794495515
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Like a <code>deephasmethod</code> 0:)</p>",
        "id": 639782072,
        "sender_full_name": "iago-lito",
        "timestamp": 1794495554
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>JET can do that kind of analysis.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Julia\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">julia</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">JET</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"nd\">@report_call</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sqrt</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"n\">No</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">errors</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">detected</span>\n\n\n<span class=\"n\">julia</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">JET</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"nd\">@report_call</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pairs</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"n\">═════</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">possible</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">error</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">found</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">═════</span>\n<span class=\"n\">┌</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pairs</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">collection</span><span class=\"o\">::</span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"p\">})</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"err\">@</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Base</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">./</span><span class=\"n\">abstractdict</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">jl</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"mi\">178</span>\n<span class=\"n\">│</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">no</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">matching</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">method</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">found</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"sb\">`keys(::Type{Type})`</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">keys</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">collection</span><span class=\"o\">::</span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"p\">})</span>\n<span class=\"n\">└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 639785331,
        "sender_full_name": "Gunnar Farnebäck",
        "timestamp": 1794496096
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>That seems.. impressive! Do you think it's resolved at compile time?</p>",
        "id": 639785901,
        "sender_full_name": "iago-lito",
        "timestamp": 1794496193
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Or that we could actually implement <code>deephasmethod</code> in terms of that <code>@report_call</code>?</p>",
        "id": 639786074,
        "sender_full_name": "iago-lito",
        "timestamp": 1794496222
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The whole point of JET is to do static analysis but it has some <a href=\"https://github.com/aviatesk/JET.jl#limitations\">limitations</a>.</p>",
        "id": 639787776,
